<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pozzuoli</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Puteoli, Dicaearchia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pozzuoli is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Founded around 530 BCE by exiles from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> as Dicaearchia, it became the Roman colony of Puteoli in 194 BCE and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s main port for trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> until Ostia was enlarged. It lies in the volcanic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campi-flegrei">Campi Flegrei</a>, and its ground still rises and falls through bradyseism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pozzuoli.jpg" alt="Pozzuoli" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: © Ra Boe / Wikipedia Create the proper attribution for your usage by clicking on this button! This file is licensed u... · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pozzuoli_2010-by-RaBoe-23.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
